WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.880
{IF YOU ARE SEEING THIS, YOUR PLAYER IS NOT RENDERING THE SUBTITLES PROPERLY. PLEASE REFER TO http://saizen-fansubs.com/?section=playback FOR THE INTENDED PLAYBACK.}

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.150
It'll be impossible to win this year as well, Miss.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:17.990
At least with Shigeno we have a really good closer.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:23.410
We improved our fielding in training camp.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.460
And our offense, as usual, is strong.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:31.800
However, we can't win with just that.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:39.180
Putting aside teamwork, the main problem is that no one aims for the championship in the Minors.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.560
It's normal for the owner of a team,
like you, to aim for the championship,

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:52.490
but most of the players on the Bats are looking for a shot to rise up to the Majors.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:55.740
"We can win in the Minor League as many times as we want,

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.700
but if we can't rise to the Majors, then there's no point."

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.660
That's what all the Triple A players are really shooting for.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.670
Isn't that what you're after too, Shigeno?

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:07.670
Y-Yeah, pretty much.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:08.960
Y-Yeah, pretty much.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.710
Isn't it the same way for you?

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.590
I'm already 34.

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:22.010
I threw away my dream of rising to the Majors a long time ago.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.060
In the Minors, these are my final hours.

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:35.950
If that's the case, then I'd like to taste victory just once with the Bats, as thanks for taking care of me for seven years.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:44.160
Even so, it's impossible to convince the youngsters.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:49.630
It's not impossible!

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.460
I understand now.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:56.010
No wonder I thought I'd teamed up with a bunch of half-hearted guys.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:02:01.260
Because they don't go for the win, they just sit around and rot.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.430
I'm going to help you, old man!

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:08.980
Let's make sure the Bats win the championship this year!

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:11.150
Shigeno!

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:53.250
Together with Sanders, aiming to win the championship, a series of eight games to start the season awaited us.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:56.090
We won the first game, but...

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.590
After that...

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:03.090
Before we could show off our vaunted batting power, losing came first.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:05.140
The result was...

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.850
two wins and six losses.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.810
With a miserable result that made us known as the last-place team in the Eastern Division,

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:13.140
we flew from Rhode Island to Albuquerque.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:21.150
Boss! What's the deal with that meeting just now!?

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.280
What do you mean?

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.450
What do you mean "what"?

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.450
When the team's been faltering since the beginning of the season, don't say:

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:32.250
"Don't worry about it. Go with high spirits and make sure you don't get hurt today either!"

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.670
You still call yourself the coach after that?

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:39.880
If you don't hold a more serious meeting, we'll be in last place by a huge margin! {Kohn- Literally he's saying "a meeting with a sense of crisis"}

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.170
A serious meeting, huh?

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.800
Well, aren't things fine as they are?

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:51.270
If we agitate them with something like that,
they'll be pressured and become even worse at hitting.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.230
Well, sooner or later we'll be able to win...

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:00.320
If the pitching and batting get in gear.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.580
Did you understand what we talked about?

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:11.450
Yeah.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:12.660
Most of it.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:15.370
We go on a losing streak every year,

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:18.840
but this year we're on one right off the bat, so it's serious.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:21.960
Well, even if we try to change things,

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.630
the coach is like that.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:27.800
If only the two of us aim for victory,

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.680
it won't be easy.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:35.850
Well, I guess both you and I will have to do our jobs perfectly.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:58.250
The score in the Vipers-Bats game is 2-2.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:00.460
It's the top of the ninth inning, and the Bats are up to bat.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:03.750
The Bats' hitting is cold today as well,

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.420
but this inning they start at the top of their lineup.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:09.840
Now hitting, number 2: Kelloge!

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.510
Kelloge! Put your spirit into it!

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:14.770
Okay, let's win this!

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.100
Since we came all the way here,

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.350
I won't forgive you if you lose!

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:34.790
Okay!

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:35.620
He did it!

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:39.580
Now hitting, number 1: Buter!

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:52.930
Foul!

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:58.180
Boss! Why are you telling him to hit here?

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:03.230
Buter's batting average this season is .100. He's in a slump!

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:06.690
In the ninth inning, with the score tied, no outs, and a runner on first...

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:09.490
No matter how I look at it, the natural thing would be to sacrifice bunt!

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.910
He's got a lot of pride,

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.490
and he's bad at bunting.

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:18.830
Making him do something like that just because he's in a slump...

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:21.290
won't help him.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.170
Look.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:31.470
Kelloge! Don't overdo it!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:32.470
Go back!

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:39.270
Out!

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:44.610
What is that idiot doing!?

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.020
Damn!

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:49.280
Damn you, what are you doing!?

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.280
This is no time to be reckless!

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.320
Shut up!

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:57.490
I didn't think the right fielder had such a good arm.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:07:59.080
Don't screw around!

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.710
You didn't even check up on something like that!?

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.170
Shut up and stop complaining, Sanders.

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:09.920
That right fielder is a newcomer this season, who was just promoted from Double A.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:14.470
We couldn't know something like that since it's only the start of the season.

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:16.550
We know now.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:21.520
And also, if the ball had strayed a little, he might've been safe.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:24.150
You've been constantly criticizing our strategies for a while now.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.940
What's with you, damn it?

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:38.030
<i>If you'd watched them practice before the game, or checked his scouting report...</i>

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:41.700
<i>you could have easily found out that he's got a good arm.</i>

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:45.170
<i>Buter's hit was a good result too.</i>

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:48.290
<i>If we could've at least gotten a runner in scoring position,</i>

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:50.710
<i>our opponents would've become very hesitant.</i>

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:08.690
Out!

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:10.150
Wha-!

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:10.980
Wha-!?

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:17.450
Out!

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:28.040
This can't be...

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:34.170
<i>Victory...</i>

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:38.470
<i>No matter how good they are at hitting, it'll stay a dream like this.</i>

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:43.470
Don't mind, don't mind.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:51.070
<i>As long as we continue to play such tasteless baseball, this is impossible.</i>

00:09:58.820 --> 00:09:59.530
Yes?

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:02.740
Hey, Kaplan, it's your turn.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.870
Oh dear, I have to pitch today too, huh?

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.420
Wait a second!

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.420
What did you say?

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:13.090
Hey, Boss!

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:19.550
Attention please, pitching, number 56:

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:22.050
Goro Shigeno!

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:22.850
Shigeno!

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:25.060
Are you sure, Boss?

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:29.150
The score's still tied; are you really going to put in the closer, Shigeno, already?

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:33.110
Well, he himself said he wanted to pitch.

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:36.650
Kaplan was feeling tired too, so it's perfect.

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.410
What are you intending to do, Shigeno?

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:43.990
The score is still tied.

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:48.410
You guys are playing a game that's irritating to watch.

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:52.670
I couldn't stand sucking my thumb and watching from the bullpen any longer.

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:55.090
You...

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:02.600
Now hitting, number 12: Garand!

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.020
<i>That Shigeno...</i>

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:13.560
<i>Stepping onto the mound when the score is tied...
What in the world are you trying to accomplish?</i>

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:19.820
Strike!

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.530
Strike two!

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.250
Strike out!

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:39.800
Strike out!

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.640
<i>So that's it, Shigeno.</i>

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:48.270
<i>You're trying to strike some spirit into our guys with soulful pitching.</i>

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:54.060
<i>With that last hit I've gone one for four, huh?</i>

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:56.980
<i>Have I risen to .200 now?</i>

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:00.240
<i>I've got to hurry and rise to .300 somehow.</i>

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:06.660
Damn!

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.700
Wait! Even if you throw, you won't make it!

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:17.920
He's done it again, that idiot!

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.920
Sorry, sorry!

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:28.260
Now hitting, number 38: Herid! {Kohn- "heriddo"}

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:35.400
Third!

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:38.270
All right, all right!

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:39.900
Out of the way!

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:43.990
Out!

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:48.450
D-Damn you... What are you doing!?

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:50.910
Sorry about that.

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:54.120
I wanted to play along nicely with you guys in the beginning,

00:12:54.120 --> 00:13:00.590
but I realized that if I count on you, neither the Bats nor I will ever be able to soar.

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:02.550
Listen clearly, you guys as well!

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:07.220
I'll make the Bats win this season and rise to the Majors no matter what!

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:12.390
I won't show any mercy to anyone who gets in the way of that ambition by playing half-heartedly!

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:15.770
Prepare yourselves, you bunch of Minor Leaguers!

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:19.690
Shigeno...

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:24.700
This is a free fansub.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:24.700
Not for sale or rent.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.330
Y-You bastard!

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:32.750
If you try to start a fight in Japanese, we won't understand you!

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:34.160
Stop it, Buter!

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:36.670
It's because you were screwing around...

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:40.130
that Shigeno went to catch that pop fly himself.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:44.280
If you wonder why he did that, try asking your own heart!

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:45.630
<i>What!?</i>

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:52.010
What was with that play, Shigeno?

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:53.720
Why did you go yourself...

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:55.270
to catch a routine pop fly to third?

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:57.850
Boss!

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:02.690
Shigeno acted like that as a protest against Buter's play.

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:07.910
Even with the sloppy attack in the top of the ninth inning,

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:09.870
he volunteered to take the mound...

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:13.290
because the team was slacking off!

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:21.290
Now hitting, number 3: Morgan!

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.670
I'm still asking, what was that?

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:29.840
Even if we, for argument's sake, say that Buter's play was half-hearted-still, what was that?

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:35.640
If Buter got injured when Shigeno did a thing like that, would he be able to take responsibility for it?

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:41.190
It's because you, the coach, aren't doing anything!

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:43.520
When the team is in such bad shape,

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.530
why are you just sitting here making a careless pose!?

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:49.820
If you want to win that badly,

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:53.780
go by yourself to another team,
or another independent league as you wish.

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:55.120
When it all comes down to it,

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:58.750
the Bats' role is a Major League regulation place for the Hornets.

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:03.920
You should've known that fact for a while now.

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:07.220
A victory in the Minors is nothing but a decoration.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:06.350
Out!

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:12.550
When summer ends, I'll call a meeting to enlarge our main force, the Major League Roster.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:15.390
To hell with teamwork.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:18.310
The task I've been requested to carry out from the higher-ups is...

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:22.940
to ensure that the players in my care aren't injured, and to make use of their strong points.

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:25.980
I'm only doing what the voices from the Majors are telling me to!

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:30.990
Ball!

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:32.070
Ball four!

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:36.950
Go.

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:39.290
It's your turn at-bat.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:44.000
Now hitting, number 8: Sanders!

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:48.420
I understand, Boss.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:49.550
But...

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.680
I wonder if guys who don't desperately focus on every victory-

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:52.800
No.

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:58.060
Every ball, every throw, every at-bat...

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:01.020
Can they really rise to the Majors?

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:10.950
Play!

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:18.410
Strike!

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:28.710
Foul!

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:32.930
<i>When I was incited by Shigeno, I understood too.</i>

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:41.140
<i>What we on the Bats, unable to rise to the Majors and rotting away here, lack...</i>

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:44.310
<i>What's even more important than better fielding or a closer...</i>

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:50.190
<i>is the attitude to really aim for victory!</i>

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:12.090
<i>Not yet!</i>

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:15.010
<i>I'm not out yet!</i>

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:21.890
S-Safe!

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:23.430
All right!

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:24.770
Safe! Safe!

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:38.830
<i>I wonder if guys who don't desperately focus on every ball, every throw, every at-bat...</i>

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:42.370
<i>can really rise to the Majors?</i>

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.630
Okay!

00:17:47.630 --> 00:17:52.050
Now hitting, number 56: Shigeno!

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.550
Boss! Aren't you going to send out a pinch hitter?

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:55.720
Play!

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:04.430
<i>Your feelings have been conveyed well enough, old man!</i>

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:08.100
<i>As I thought, there's no meaning in playing a game if the team...</i>

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:09.360
<i>doesn't win!</i>

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:15.490
Foul!

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.200
So close!

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.870
T-That bastard...

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:23.240
despite being a pitcher, he bats so well!

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:27.080
<i>Damn it, this guy's dangerous!</i>

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:30.670
<i>If I go easy on him for being a pitcher, I'm done for!</i>

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:34.460
<i>Okay, scare him with one high and inside!</i>

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:54.900
Dead ball!

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:55.530
Shigeno!

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:56.860
H-Hey!

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:00.660
Are you all right, Shigeno?

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:02.450
Are you hurt?

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:05.290
Okay, okay! No problems!

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:08.620
An injury like this will heal with just some spit.

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:11.750
Forget about that, the bases are loaded.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.290
I'm counting on you, Roy!

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:14.550
Y-You...

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:15.760
Y-You...

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:18.840
It can't be that you didn't dodge it on purpose?

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:32.980
Geez, a southpaw allowing the ball to hit his left arm...

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:36.280
Normally, you'd evade that unconsciously.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:42.530
<i>It doesn't matter that there's no meaning in winning the Triple A championship.</i>

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:44.950
<i>But, if everyone tries their best...</i>

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:47.450
<i>to win the game,</i>

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:50.000
<i>we'll naturally get closer to our goal.</i>

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:55.880
<i>What we on the Bats, unable to rise to the Majors and rotting away here, lack...</i>

00:19:55.880 --> 00:20:01.340
<i>is the attitude to really aim for victory!</i>

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:10.480
Now hitting, number 4: Roy!

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:18.150
<i>What we on the Bats, rotting away here, lack...</i>

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:21.150
<i>Okay!</i>

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:22.820
<i>I just have to aim to win.</i>

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:28.040
Roy bunted!?

00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:41.630
They did it!

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:43.590
Yes!

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:45.720
All right! Well done, Roy!

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:47.350
Nice squeeze!

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:51.270
Who would've thought that swing-loving Roy would bunt?

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:52.730
It's the first time I've seen it.

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:58.440
How uncool!

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:01.280
That was totally out of character.

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:06.070
Now hitting, number 2: Kelloge!

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:07.330
All right!

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:08.990
Keep it going, Kelloge!

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.000
Ball!

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:22.550
Ball!

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:29.100
Ball! Ball four!

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:31.060
All right!

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:32.270
Damn it!

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:33.730
Okay!

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:42.610
Now hitting, number 1: Buter!

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:48.030
Hey!

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:50.620
He's choking up on the bat!

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:52.160
Buter is?

00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:57.500
<i>Victory, huh?</i>

00:21:57.880 --> 00:21:58.960
<i>It can't be helped.</i>

00:21:59.590 --> 00:22:01.550
<i>I guess I'll really aim for it!</i>

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:34.790
<i>I have a good feeling about this!</i>

00:22:34.790 --> 00:22:37.830
<i>This year... it feels like it could actually work!</i>

00:24:10.930 --> 00:24:11.880
What!?

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:16.390
Coach Ando has strained his back before the game against Yokohama Little again!?

00:24:16.390 --> 00:24:17.350
Komori,

00:24:17.350 --> 00:24:19.680
you've got to be the coach in his place!

00:24:19.680 --> 00:24:23.020
Make that sunglass-sporting old man speechless!

00:24:23.020 --> 00:24:23.980
Next time, on Major:

00:24:24.400 --> 00:24:25.150
Liar!

00:24:25.650 --> 00:24:28.030
Run to the stage of your dreams!
